Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:41:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 347/389] Assembly: big steps of a driven angle are walked by
 value; any angle; reverse kept

From the second whole-engine GUI test (0.7.8):
- A big step of a driven angle (a crank from 0 to 390, or 200 to 600
  degrees) is walked through by the angle's value in steps of 15
  degrees: by the placement, 0 to 390 was a turn of 30 and a 28/14
  chain's cam took the other half turn, kept even back at 0.
- A joint's Angle has no limit (it stopped at 360 though the panel took
  more): 720 degrees is a four-stroke cycle.
- The panel's angle and distance are solved when the number is done
  (Enter or leaving the field), not at each digit: 300 typed after 270
  solved 3 first and stayed there.
- "Reverse" is counted (FlipCount): an axis turned over by it is not
  taken as the solver's wrong answer, and a slider moved to a distance
  may be turned half a turn (a valve put upright was taken as broken).

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve, -t TestAssemblyWorkbench

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
